Modifications (version 0.8.1-mod.1, 2026-11):

  * Title resolution now folds the last `session/title` event by scanning back to
    frame 6, instead of only looking at a bounded 160-frame tail window. Results
    are cached by `mtime:size` and persisted to disk.
  * Session-list reads are concurrent (16-way), headers are read once per scan,
    and sessions >= 2 KB are no longer decompressed to decide whether they are
    blank.
  * Recycle-bin retention copy corrected to 15 days; the produced-file warning
    corrected to state that files are moved into the bin and restored with the
    session.
  * Startup reconciliation and retention purge are deferred by 15 seconds, and
    both timers are unref()ed, so the plugin stays off the host's startup I/O path.

Title resolution also draws on ideas and API-usage patterns from:

  xohmai/dsh-session-delete
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  A copy of that license is included at licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

  Specifically: reading titles through the host `sessionProjectionCache`
  (`cachedSnapshot` / `cachedPredecessorTitle`, with `isSeeded` normalised to
  false), and the two caveats that (a) `sessionQuery.readTitleSnapshots` must be
  called in a single batch because a per-id call is near-quadratic, and (b) its
  `title` is a snapshot object rather than a string.

No source code is copied from DeepSeek Harness itself. Its published interfaces
were read for interoperability only; DeepSeek Harness is MIT-licensed.
